LayaStudio
https://github.com/biplovgautam/LayaStudio (Apache-2.0)

The Snake benchmark task in scripts/snake_cpu_bench.py is adapted from layastudio/snake.py: the move
question text and options (QUESTIONS), the text board state (render), the free-space count
(free_space) and the planner teacher (teacher) are reproduced with formatting changes only, and
protocol_b follows its `play` and `summarize` functions. The planner-game generator `generate` in
glance/snake.py follows its `generate` function (same seed scheme, 20% exploration, 400-tick cap).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Hugging Face Transformers
https://github.com/huggingface/transformers (Apache-2.0)
Copyright 2024 Answer.AI, LightOn, and contributors, and the HuggingFace Inc. team.
Copyright 2024 the HuggingFace Inc. team.

glance/mlx/modernbert.py is an MLX port of the ModernBERT encoder in
transformers/models/modernbert/modeling_modernbert.py (layer structure, GLU MLP, per-layer-type
rotary embeddings). The pixel-shuffle connector in scripts/latency_mlx.py follows
Idefics3Connector.pixel_shuffle in transformers/models/idefics3/modeling_idefics3.py, as used by
ModernVBERT. The single-tower layers in glance/model/towers.py and glance/mlx/tower.py keep the
module layout and parameter names of the SigLIP vision encoder in
transformers/models/siglip/modeling_siglip.py so that its weights load directly.

